e non-negative).\n        \"\"\"\n        if amount < 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Cannot add negative mana: {amount}\")\n        self._pool[mana_type] = self._pool.get(mana_type, 0) + amount\n\n    def empty(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Clear the pool — happens at phase/step transitions.\"\"\"\n        for mt in self._pool:\n            self._pool[mt] = 0\n        for mt in self._restricted_pool:\n            self._restricted_pool[mt] = 0\n\n    def total(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the total amount of mana in the pool across all types.\"\"\"\n        return sum(self._pool.values()) + sum(self._restricted_pool.values())\n\n    def get(self, mana_type: ManaType) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the amount of a specific mana type in the pool.\"\"\"\n        return self._pool.get(mana_type, 0)\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Restricted mana (\"spend this mana only to cast an instant or\n    # sorcery spell\")\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def add_restricted(self, mana_type: ManaType, amount: int = 1) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Add mana that may only be spent casting instant/sorcery spells.\"\"\"\n        if amount < 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Cannot add negative mana: {amount}\")\n        self._restricted_pool[mana_type] = (\n            self._restricted_pool.get(mana_type, 0) + amount\n        )\n\n    def get_restricted(self, mana_type: ManaType) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the amount of restricted mana of the given type.\"\"\"\n        return self._restricted_pool.get(mana_type, 0)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _restriction_allows(spell: Any) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Return True if restricted mana may pay for *spell*.\"\"\"\n        from engine.types import CardType\n\n        if spell is None:\n            return False\n        card_types = getattr(spell, \"card_types\", set())\n        return bool({CardType.INSTANT, CardType.SORCERY} & card_types)\n\n    def _available(self, spell: Any) -> dict[ManaType, int]:\n        \"\"\"Return the mana usable to pay for *spell* (merged when eligible).\"\"\"\n        if self._restriction_allows(spell):\n            return {\n                mt: self._pool.get(mt, 0) + self._restricted_pool.get(mt, 0)\n                for mt in ManaType\n            }\n        return dict(self._pool)\n\n    @property\n    def last_payment_colors(self) -> list[Color]:\n        \"\"\"Return the distinct colors of mana spent in the last :meth:`pay` call.\n\n        Colorless mana is not a color and is excluded.  The list is sorted\n        by Color enum order for determinism.  Empty if no payment has been\n        made or if all mana spent was colorless.\n        \"\"\"\n        return list(self._last_payment_colors)\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Cost payment\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def can_pay(self, cost: ManaCost, spell: Any | None = None) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check whether the pool can satisfy *cost*.\n\n        Generic mana can be paid by any type.  X is treated as 0 for\n        ``can_pay`` unless explicitly set in the cost's generic component.\n        Hybrid symbols can be paid with either option; this method uses\n        backtracking to find a valid assignment.\n\n        Parameters:\n            cost: The mana cost to check.\n            spell: The spell being paid for, if any.  Restricted mana\n                (instant/sorcery-only) is counted only when *spell* is an\n                instant or sorcery.\n\n        Returns:\n            True if the pool has enough mana to pay the cost.\n        \"\"\"\n        remaining: dict[ManaType, int] = self._available(spell)\n\n        # Pay colored/colorless pips first.\n        for mana_type, count in cost.pips.items():\n            if remaining.get(mana_type, 0) < count:\n                return False\n            remaining[